in @prism

in @mirror/glass/ast

# @mirror/glass/ast/shape — the canonical type for top-level
# declarations inside a glass block.
#
# Substrate-altitude decisions resolved 2026-05-26 (Alex + Reed):
#
#   - `shape` replaces `form` as the type name for the canonical
#     top-level declaration variants. `form` was overloaded:
#     sometimes a noun ("the IO form"), sometimes a choice combinator
#     ("refract form = choice(...)"). The split dissolves: the noun
#     is `shape`; the choice combinator is gone (the type structure
#     IS the choice).
#
# Variant rationale:
#
#   - `glass` (replaces `grammar`): the substrate primitive itself —
#     `grammar @<name>(<tags>) { <body> }` at file root.
#   - `type`: a `type <name>(...)` declaration body.
#   - `lambda` (replaces `action`): the binding form for an action /
#     function-like surface. `action` was OOP-ish drift; `lambda` is
#     FP-canonical (we already write `λsh` for the shell lambda).
#     `io` is an attribute on `lambda`, not a separate variant.
#   - `property`: a `property <name>(...)` declaration (the verdict-
#     returning checks at @epistemologic/property altitude).
#   - `fixed` (new): the new module-top binding keyword. Per Alex
#     2026-05-26: "`fixed`. Like `const`. But math. And a `fixed`
#     value cannot include any holes. No inference. It needs to be
#     a fully settled crystal. Becomes content addressed." The
#     binding IS the crystal IS the OID. Distinct from `beam` (body-
#     altitude, dynamic, may carry Beam<T> metadata).
#   - `in`: import boundary declaration (`in @<ref>`).
#   - `out`: export boundary declaration (`out @<ref>`).
#
# Dropped from the legacy variant list:
#
#   - `match_form` / `select_form`: per spec design call #87, these
#     are body-altitude (expression position), not shape-altitude.
#     They appear INSIDE a lambda body, not at the top of a glass.
#   - `refract_form`: drift per the 8-category audit (Cat 7);
#     migrates to `fixed` via @kintsugi/fracture/refract-to-fixed
#     (#96). The legacy `refract <name> = <combinator>` lines in
#     grammar.mirror and nl.mirror lift to `fixed` in that tick.
#   - `op_decl`: `op` is not a keyword in mirror (Mara's notation
#     in the legacy file; corrected per the 2026-05-26 audit). The
#     five operations are recognized at lex time via the keyword
#     table; they don't need a separate shape variant.
#
# Future structure for each variant (when its body becomes
# substantial) lands under @mirror/glass/ast/shape/<variant>.

grammar @mirror/glass/ast/shape {
  # The seven canonical top-level declaration variants. No leading
  # `|`; no Java-style redundant naming; each variant IS the keyword.
  type shape = glass | type | lambda | property | fixed | in | out
}

out shape
out @mirror/glass/ast/shape
